<section class="card"><div class="migration-mark">SQL Server <span>→</span> SQLite</div><h2>Create a SQLite database</h2>
    <p>Export tables, supported views, and procedure scripts from the current SQL Server database.</p>
    <div class="callout">Keep the generated <strong>StoredProcedures</strong> folder alongside the output database. Unsupported SQL is reported in the conversion results.</div>
    <p class="muted">Progress appears in the status bar. You can request cancellation while conversion is running. A canceled or failed conversion may leave an incomplete database.</p>
    <div class="actions"><button class="primary" @onclick="W.ConvertSqliteAsync">Choose destination and convert</button></div>
</section>
@code { [CascadingParameter] public WorkspaceController W { get; set; } = default!; }
